{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "OctoPrint-Enclosure API",
    "description": "The API is located at `<OctoPrint URL>/plugin/enclosure`.\n\nA failed request answers with an error status code and the body `{\"errors\": [string]}`, with one message for each problem found.\n\n## Permissions\n\nEach endpoint needs a permission of the plugin. OctoPrint gives the permissions to groups and users (OctoPrint Settings > Access Control), and a request has the permissions of its user, e.g. the user of its API key.\n\n| Permission | Key | Description | Default groups |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Status | `PLUGIN_ENCLOSURE_STATUS` | Allows to see inputs, outputs, actions and automations, with their state. | `admins`, `users`, `readonly` |\n| Control outputs | `PLUGIN_ENCLOSURE_OUTPUTS_CONTROL` | Allows to turn outputs on and off, and to set their duty cycle, color or target. Includes the \"Status\" permission. | `admins`, `users` |\n| Run actions | `PLUGIN_ENCLOSURE_ACTIONS_RUN` | Allows to run actions, e.g. G-code or shell scripts. Includes the \"Status\" permission. | `admins`, `users` |\n| Enable and disable automations | `PLUGIN_ENCLOSURE_AUTOMATIONS_ENABLE` | Allows to enable and disable automations. Includes the \"Status\" permission. | `admins`, `users` |\n\n## Push messages\n\nThe plugin also sends its state over the OctoPrint push websocket, as plugin messages of the plugin `enclosure`, to the users with the Status permission. A message has one of these attributes:\n\n- `inputs`: the same list as `GET /inputs`\n- `outputs`: the same list as `GET /outputs`\n- `automations`: the same list as `GET /automations`",
    "version": "4.13.2"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "{octoprint}/plugin/enclosure",
      "variables": {
        "octoprint": {
          "default": "http://127.0.0.1:5000",
          "description": "The URL of OctoPrint."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Inputs",
      "description": "The HTTP API of the inputs."
    },
    {
      "name": "Outputs",
      "description": "The HTTP API of the outputs."
    },
    {
      "name": "Actions",
      "description": "The HTTP API of the actions."
    },
    {
      "name": "Automations",
      "description": "The HTTP API of the automations."
    },
    {
      "name": "Documentation",
      "description": "The documentation of the API."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/inputs": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Inputs"
        ],
        "summary": "List the inputs, ordered by id, with their state.",
        "description": "Needs the \"Status\" permission.",
        "operationId": "get_inputs",
        "security": [
          {
            "apiKey": [
              "PLUGIN_ENCLOSURE_STATUS"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "A JSON list.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InputResponse"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "The user doesn't have the permission.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
